   "concept": {
    "name": "Last Bus Stop",
    "tagline": "The bus is late, and nothing needs you until it comes.",
    "brief": "Rain taps the tin roof in a slow, uneven rhythm while frogs and the last cicadas fill the paddies, so the mind has one soft thing to follow, as Mary Oliver would say. Breathe in the wet grass and warm earth, count the drops from the eave, and let the thoughts drift off like the road into the dusk.",
    "image_prompt": "A small weathered wooden bus shelter with a tin roof and a plain ash-wood bench, standing alone on a gravel road beside flooded rice paddies at dusk in gentle summer rain. A huge camphor tree rises behind it, its leaves dripping. Puddles reflect lavender-grey clouds and a thin gold line near the horizon. A blank round sign on a slim pole, a clear plastic umbrella hooked on the bench end, a small paper-wrapped parcel tied with twine on the seat, tall wet grass and fireflies in the paddies. Photoreal wide shot at eye level.",
